tal role in nurturing community spirit, celebrating our cultural heritage, and boosting tourism in County Carlow. The Festival and Events Grant Scheme is a key initiative that empowers organisers to create enriching, high-quality experiences that contribute to the local economy while showcasing all that Carlow has to offer. I urge all eligible groups to apply and turn their creative visions into reality.\u201d The portal will close for applications on 27th February, 2026 and is applicable to events scheduled between June and October 2026. This scheme is open to non-commercial groups or organisations hosting events within County Carlow only. Linda Culleton, Economic Development Officer at Carlow County Council, underscored the importance of this scheme, saying, \u201cOur aim is to provide valuable support to festival and event organisers dedicated to enhancing Carlow\u2019s tourism offerings. This scheme is crafted to help develop events that yield economic, social, and cultural advantages for the county. We are particularly interested in innovative initiatives that enliven public spaces and attract visitors from outside the region. With funding opportunities ranging from \u20ac750 for smaller, family-oriented events to as much as \u20ac5,000 for larger tourism festivals, we are eager to see a diverse range of applications.\u201d Funding Categories Small Scale Festival & Events \u2013 Family Focus Fund : Up to \u20ac750 per event (maximum 75% funding) for single-day events that deliver engaging visitor experiences. Large Scale Tourism Festival Funding : Up to \u20ac5,000 per event (maximum 75% funding) for festivals demonstrating significant tourism and economic impact, including attracting a minimum of 400 ticketed visitors and implementing regional and national marketing strategies. Applications will be assessed based on their capacity to generate economic and social benefits, their alignment with Carlow\u2019s event calendar, and their financial sustainability. Interested organizations are encouraged to review the eligibility criteria and submit their applications online prior to the deadline. For more information and application form Economic Development - Carlow County Council Festival & Event Fund 2026 | Carlow County Council's Online Consultation Portal Please contact Economic Team 059-9129783 or enterprise@carlowcoco.ie (link sends email) for any queries. Get In Touch Carlow County Council, Athy Road, Carlow. R93 E7R7 Monday \u2013 Friday : 9.15am \u2013 4.30pm Motor Tax Monday to Friday 10.00am - 12.30pm Phone: 059 9170300 Contact Us Office Locations Statutory Obligations Bye Laws Freedom of Information (link is external) Statutory Notices Ethics Declaration Regulation of Lobbying Act 2015 Reuse of Information Business Local Enterprise Office (link is external) Property Portal (link is external) InCarlow (link is external) Consultation Portal Business Supports Housekeeping Accessibility Cookie Policy Customer Complaints Privacy Policy Disclaimer Update Cookie Preferences"
